+ *
+ * The 6.18 prepared kernel has no <linux/hdcp_qseecom.h> and no QSEECom HDCP
+ * TZ transport driver.  The downstream display tree includes this header from
+ * techpack/display/msm/sde_hdcp.h only.  An actual call-site audit of the
+ * include consumers shows that neither sde_hdcp.h nor the DP/eDP HDCP 2.2
+ * transport (dp/dp_hdcp2p2.c) references any symbol from this vendor header;
+ * the HDCP TZ command surface used by sde_hdcp_2x.c comes from
+ * <linux/msm_hdcp.h> (in-tree minimal port) and local headers.
+ *
+ * PROVENANCE / LIMITS (recorded in STATUS.json):
+ *  - No declarations are invented here: the file only satisfies the include
+ *    path so the owned consumers can be compiled and audited.
+ *  - The QSEECom-backed HDCP TrustZone firmware interface is absent from the
+ *    6.18 kernel.  Any consumer that later needs it must not treat this header
+ *    as equivalent to the vendor one; sde_hdcp_1x.c / sde_hdcp_2x.c are only
+ *    partly unblocked (see VERIFICATION.txt).
+ *  - hardware_validated = false; HDCP 1.x/2.2 is unvalidated.
